# KRAV MAGA

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physical, physiological, biomechanical, tactical and psychological demands of Krav Maga.

Unlike competitive combat sports, Krav Maga is a self-defense system.

Its objective is not competitive victory.

Its objective is survival.

The Combat Athlete System (CAS) uses this model to individualize physical preparation for practitioners whose goal is maximizing real-world defensive capability.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Krav Maga is a modern self-defense system designed to maximize survivability during violent encounters.

The practitioner must rapidly identify threats,

neutralize immediate danger,

create an opportunity to escape,

and minimize unnecessary risk.

Winning is not the objective.

Survival is.

---

# Philosophy

Every action should increase the probability of survival.

Avoidance is preferable to confrontation.

Escape is preferable to domination.

Neutralization is preferable to prolonged engagement.

The objective is to end violence as rapidly as possible.

---

# Primary Objectives

The practitioner should be capable of:

